WEBVTT

00:00:17.792 --> 00:00:21.375
We will begin
the spider's nest investigation now.

00:00:21.375 --> 00:00:23.082
Yes.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:35.332
(Reincarnated as a Sword)

00:01:54.667 --> 00:01:58.250
(Episode 10
The Trap of Trap Spiders)

00:01:58.875 --> 00:02:02.167
It looks like a dungeon, all right.

00:02:02.167 --> 00:02:03.375
(Dungeon Spider's Nest,
The First Floor Underground)

00:02:03.375 --> 00:02:05.957
Spider's nest.
The First Floor Underground.

00:02:05.957 --> 00:02:08.875
It's a floor filled
with stone pillars and obstacles,

00:02:08.875 --> 00:02:12.125
making it a habitat infested
with spider monsters.

00:02:12.125 --> 00:02:14.500
The advance party's primary responsibility

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:18.250
is to scout the area and clear the path.

00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:19.292
Got it.

00:02:19.292 --> 00:02:21.375
(The Advance Party, E-Rank Party, Dragon's Roar)
Don't let your guard down.

00:02:21.375 --> 00:02:23.750
(Dragon's Roar Party Member, Gennel)
Leave it to us!

00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:25.625
(Dragon's Roar Party Member, Bart)
We're all fired up.

00:02:25.625 --> 00:02:27.500
(Dragon's Roar Party Member, Bart)
Right, Victor?

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:28.332
(Dragon's Roar Party Member, Victor)
Right.

00:02:28.332 --> 00:02:32.207
(Dragon's Roar Party Member, Victor)
Let's show them what we're made of!

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:35.957
Well, they've got a lot of gusto.

00:02:35.957 --> 00:02:39.375
(Rear Guard, E-Rank Party, Forest Eyes"
Spider monsters? How unpleasant.

00:02:39.375 --> 00:02:41.417
I don't want them near me.

00:02:41.417 --> 00:02:44.500
An adventurer is
not supposed to be scared of bugs.

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:48.125
(Forest Eyes Party Leader, Furion)
Concentrate on securing our rear defenses.

00:02:48.125 --> 00:02:50.082
(Forest Eyes Party Leader, Furion)
I'm counting on you guys.

00:02:50.082 --> 00:02:53.625
(Amanda, A-Rank Adventurer)
The spider's nest… I remember now.

00:02:54.582 --> 00:02:59.000
This dungeon was quite popular
when I first became an adventurer.

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:00.625
"We'll be the first to clear the dungeon!"

00:03:00.625 --> 00:03:03.125
This place was crowded with adventurers
who wanted to be the first to clear it.

00:03:03.125 --> 00:03:07.125
But there were also many
who lost their lives here.

00:03:07.125 --> 00:03:10.750
Many of them were parents.

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:11.792
As a result,

00:03:11.792 --> 00:03:15.000
the number of orphans in Alessa increased,

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:18.582
and that led to my opening an orphanage.

00:03:18.582 --> 00:03:21.375
Did you earn a lot because you're strong?

00:03:21.375 --> 00:03:23.167
Not at all.

00:03:23.167 --> 00:03:26.042
I was a weakling back then,
so I hardly brought in any money.

00:03:26.042 --> 00:03:28.457
I received a lot of help
from the people in the city.

00:03:28.457 --> 00:03:31.125
You'll have to cut your little chit-chat short.

00:03:33.082 --> 00:03:34.750
Monsters detected at ten o'clock!

00:03:34.750 --> 00:03:36.750
We've got them at five o'clock in the rear too!

00:03:36.750 --> 00:03:38.832
Spider monsters encountered!

00:03:38.832 --> 00:03:41.500
Oh, they're coming from the side too.

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:43.207
We've been surrounded.

00:03:44.707 --> 00:03:46.375
(Trap Spider, Lv. 6)
Trap Spiders, huh?

00:03:46.375 --> 00:03:47.875
Not a big deal.

00:03:47.875 --> 00:03:50.707
(Skills: Trap Perception 2, Trap Setting 1)
I'll take care of all these bugs.

00:03:51.207 --> 00:03:52.542
Let's do this!

00:03:52.542 --> 00:03:54.417
Dragon's Roar!

00:03:54.417 --> 00:03:55.875
Take this!

00:03:59.542 --> 00:04:01.417
Flank them!

00:04:01.417 --> 00:04:02.707
Roger!

00:04:05.582 --> 00:04:07.582
Take this, you pest!

00:04:09.957 --> 00:04:12.042
Get them, Krad!

00:04:12.042 --> 00:04:13.542
Double Spear!

00:04:14.667 --> 00:04:17.333
Dragon…

00:04:17.333 --> 00:04:19.166
Roar!

00:04:19.166 --> 00:04:21.708
Krad!

00:04:21.708 --> 00:04:24.000
We won't need your help.

00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:26.375
That's fine with us.

00:04:26.375 --> 00:04:27.833
(C-Rank Party, Azure Guardians)
All right!

00:04:30.625 --> 00:04:32.250
(Party Leader, Cruise Riouselle)
Trap Spiders

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:35.333
aren't particularly strong,

00:04:35.333 --> 00:04:38.291
but the threads they spit
can be tricky to deal with.

00:04:38.291 --> 00:04:41.166
If you get caught in the gossamer,
you'll be immobilized.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:44.375
But they're weak to fire,

00:04:44.375 --> 00:04:46.500
so you just have to burn them.

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:47.416
Mm.

00:04:47.416 --> 00:04:49.375
(Azure Guardians Party Member, Eizelle)
Their threads are actually

00:04:49.375 --> 00:04:52.083
worth quite a bit as materials.

00:04:52.083 --> 00:04:54.791
It would be a waste to burn them.

00:04:54.791 --> 00:04:56.041
Oh, I see.

00:04:56.041 --> 00:04:58.833
So let's avoid using fire if we can.

00:04:58.833 --> 00:05:00.666
That's why we would appreciate it

00:05:00.666 --> 00:05:02.833
if you could handle this
more delicately, Miss Fran.

00:05:03.875 --> 00:05:07.500
Has my Fran been labeled a pyromaniac?

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:09.375
(Dungeon Spider's Nest,
The Second Floor Underground)

00:05:09.375 --> 00:05:11.000
The second floor underground.

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:13.791
The layout on this floor
gets a little more complicated.

00:05:13.791 --> 00:05:18.083
You'll find other insect-type monsters
in addition to spiders here.

00:05:18.083 --> 00:05:19.541
(Advance Party, Forest Eyes)
So best be on guard at all times.

00:05:20.541 --> 00:05:22.041
Amanda.

00:05:22.041 --> 00:05:23.083
Yes?

00:05:23.083 --> 00:05:26.916
I want to ask you
about skills, techniques, and magic.

00:05:27.875 --> 00:05:31.250
I'm surprised to see Fran
seeking Amanda's help proactively.

00:05:31.250 --> 00:05:34.833
I can use them,
but I don't really know what they are.

00:05:34.833 --> 00:05:37.500
You're relying on me already!

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:39.500
Could I get a hug, then?

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:40.916
That's not necessary.

00:05:40.916 --> 00:05:48.125
But indeed I'm also interested in
how other adventurers perceive and learn them.

00:05:48.125 --> 00:05:50.166
First, combat techniques.

00:05:50.166 --> 00:05:56.250
Combat techniques are used by manipulating
the strength through mana inside your body.

00:05:56.250 --> 00:05:58.958
They are said to have originated
from the God of Combat and the God of Martial Arts.

00:05:59.916 --> 00:06:00.958
Krad!

00:06:00.958 --> 00:06:03.333
The monster is headed your way!

00:06:03.333 --> 00:06:05.041
Leave this to me!

00:06:05.041 --> 00:06:07.500
It's mine!

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:08.583
Spear Technique!

00:06:10.333 --> 00:06:12.458
Power Swing.

00:06:12.458 --> 00:06:14.708
That was a combat technique.

00:06:14.708 --> 00:06:19.000
My whip technique and your sword technique
belong to the same category too.

00:06:20.583 --> 00:06:24.083
I want to learn
how to train or memorize them.

00:06:24.083 --> 00:06:26.666
Well, skills and techniques are gained

00:06:26.666 --> 00:06:30.500
when the mana flowing in your body converges,

00:06:30.500 --> 00:06:34.291
like, during training or
when in combat as you use them.

00:06:34.291 --> 00:06:36.625
Power Swing!

00:06:37.208 --> 00:06:39.958
You'll feel as if you've been struck
by a divine oracle.

00:06:40.708 --> 00:06:42.666
I'm sure you must have
experienced that too, Fran.

00:06:42.666 --> 00:06:44.166
I don't remember.

00:06:44.166 --> 00:06:45.500
Oh, dear.

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:47.083
Well, that's only natural.

00:06:47.083 --> 00:06:51.875
After all, for her, she was suddenly able
to use the level 7 sword technique on that day.

00:06:54.291 --> 00:07:00.041
You might be able to pick things up faster
if you study under a master of your class.

00:07:00.041 --> 00:07:04.375
That's right!
I do learn things faster with a "teacher"!

00:07:04.375 --> 00:07:07.500
I don't think you're talking about the same thing...

00:07:07.500 --> 00:07:09.208
(Dungeon Spider's Nest,
The Third Floor Underground)

00:07:09.208 --> 00:07:10.875
The third floor underground.

00:07:10.875 --> 00:07:13.833
There are fewer places to hide here,

00:07:13.833 --> 00:07:16.333
which also means fewer monsters.

00:07:16.333 --> 00:07:19.583
Finally, we're in the open.

00:07:19.583 --> 00:07:22.041
We can finally get some air
in this enclosed space.

00:07:23.083 --> 00:07:24.500
A trap!

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:25.916
Sorry, Krad!

00:07:27.208 --> 00:07:30.375
There'll be more traps starting from this floor.

00:07:30.375 --> 00:07:32.791
Tell us that sooner!

00:07:32.791 --> 00:07:35.125
Do you press this to disable the traps?

00:07:35.125 --> 00:07:36.916
Don't touch that!

00:07:41.416 --> 00:07:42.958
No!

00:07:42.958 --> 00:07:44.625
Saw this coming…

00:07:44.625 --> 00:07:47.083
Calm down, everyone!

00:07:52.166 --> 00:07:53.666
That sure hurts…

00:07:53.666 --> 00:07:56.375
Eizelle, disable the traps, please.

00:07:56.375 --> 00:07:57.625
Got it.

00:07:57.625 --> 00:07:59.791
Next, skills.

00:07:59.791 --> 00:08:00.916
Please.

00:08:01.875 --> 00:08:04.916
Trap Detection.

00:08:06.083 --> 00:08:11.000
It is said that skills are a divine craft
bestowed upon our souls by the world

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:15.250
once we've trained enough and possessed
required proficiency in a certain field.

00:08:16.458 --> 00:08:20.166
I've disarmed all the traps in our path.

00:08:22.041 --> 00:08:24.708
Trap Detection looks useful. I want that.

00:08:24.708 --> 00:08:26.125
Indeed.

00:08:26.125 --> 00:08:30.500
I'm sure it'll come in handy
when we take on dungeons by ourselves.

00:08:30.500 --> 00:08:33.292
Apart from ordinary skills,

00:08:33.292 --> 00:08:36.832
some unique skills and extra skills

00:08:36.832 --> 00:08:40.625
seem to be granted to us
by the gods according to their whims.

00:08:40.625 --> 00:08:43.042
All of these are categorized as skills,

00:08:43.042 --> 00:08:46.417
but it appears that not all of them
can be standardized.

00:08:47.582 --> 00:08:49.625
Lastly, magic.

00:08:49.625 --> 00:08:54.207
Magic is a kind of trick that needs you
to manipulate your inner mana and output it.

00:08:54.207 --> 00:09:00.125
There are four basic elements.
Earth, water, fire, and wind.

00:09:00.125 --> 00:09:05.457
The advanced version of each element would be
ground, ocean, inferno, and storm, respectively.

00:09:05.457 --> 00:09:07.750
We've acquired the four basic elements

00:09:07.750 --> 00:09:12.082
and the advanced version
of fire magic, inferno magic.

00:09:12.082 --> 00:09:13.707
When you want to learn or train in magic,

00:09:13.707 --> 00:09:18.167
you must first know
the element you are compatible with.

00:09:18.167 --> 00:09:20.082
For instance, to learn water magic,

00:09:20.082 --> 00:09:23.000
you should surround yourself
with water, embrace it,

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:26.582
and infuse the image
of water into your body and soul.

00:09:26.582 --> 00:09:29.000
Become one with the water

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:31.000
to the point where you even dream of it,

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:32.750
and you'll have mastered the water magic.

00:09:32.750 --> 00:09:36.082
If you aren't compatible with it, however,
you won't get far, no matter how much you train.

00:09:36.082 --> 00:09:37.792
I see.

00:09:37.792 --> 00:09:42.750
To master earth magic, you'll need
to bury yourself and even consume dirt.

00:09:42.750 --> 00:09:44.292
- That's tough!
- That's tough!

00:09:44.292 --> 00:09:46.667
What about wind magic like yours, Amanda?

00:09:46.667 --> 00:09:48.250
It's terribly boring.

00:09:48.250 --> 00:09:52.542
You'll need to bathe in the wind
and allow yourself to be wrapped in the breeze.

00:09:52.542 --> 00:09:53.707
Fully naked.

00:09:53.707 --> 00:09:55.042
Naked?

00:09:55.042 --> 00:09:58.250
All right. I'll try that.

00:09:58.250 --> 00:09:59.417
What?

00:09:59.417 --> 00:10:01.750
Not on my watch, Fran!

00:10:02.792 --> 00:10:06.375
We'll be descending the stairs
to the fourth floor after this point.

00:10:08.625 --> 00:10:11.167
They are more than the report said.

00:10:11.917 --> 00:10:14.957
The Forest Eyes will take lead.

00:10:14.957 --> 00:10:17.125
We'll split up and eliminate them.

00:10:17.125 --> 00:10:18.500
Once we've gotten them down to a certain number,

00:10:18.500 --> 00:10:20.875
we'll leave the rest to the other parties.

00:10:20.875 --> 00:10:22.582
Got it!

00:10:22.582 --> 00:10:25.250
Then, there's also complex magic.

00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:27.707
Complex magic?

00:10:27.707 --> 00:10:29.750
It's a type of magic you might learn

00:10:29.750 --> 00:10:33.082
if you're getting good at two elements or more.

00:10:33.082 --> 00:10:36.082
Wood Magic! Trunk Shot!

00:10:38.250 --> 00:10:42.292
That is wood magic,
a combination of water and earth magic.

00:10:42.292 --> 00:10:45.375
Furion and the guild master are both wood elves.

00:10:45.375 --> 00:10:47.750
They're born with earth and water magic.

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:50.875
So they don't need their earth and water
magic levels to be that high to use wood magic.

00:10:52.292 --> 00:10:55.042
Furion looks normal but he's actually so good.

00:10:55.042 --> 00:10:56.292
Looks normal?

00:10:56.292 --> 00:10:58.707
There are other types of complex magic as well.

00:10:58.707 --> 00:11:01.375
With water and wind, you get frost.

00:11:01.375 --> 00:11:04.332
Water and fire create life.

00:11:04.332 --> 00:11:06.917
Wind and fire make thunder.

00:11:06.917 --> 00:11:09.625
Wind and earth make dust.

00:11:09.625 --> 00:11:12.375
Earth and fire create molten magic.

00:11:12.375 --> 00:11:15.250
Thunder! That sounds strong!

00:11:15.250 --> 00:11:19.125
Fran, you can use fire,
earth, and wind magic, right?

00:11:20.292 --> 00:11:24.792
If you keep getting better at wind and fire magic,
you might just be able to acquire thunder magic.

00:11:24.792 --> 00:11:26.875
Really?

00:11:26.875 --> 00:11:30.207
It's rare for someone to be able
to use more than two elements.

00:11:30.207 --> 00:11:33.207
Much less three…

00:11:33.207 --> 00:11:37.957
I've tried to master fire magic as well,
but I was never able to advance far.

00:11:37.957 --> 00:11:41.457
Oh, dear… Those with two are already rare?

00:11:41.457 --> 00:11:43.292
(Dungeon Spider's Nest,
The Forth Floor Underground)

00:11:43.292 --> 00:11:45.917
Let's take a short break.

00:11:45.917 --> 00:11:49.667
This floor is structured in a way
that makes it hard for monsters to approach.

00:11:49.667 --> 00:11:52.292
So this floor is something like a save point?

00:11:52.292 --> 00:11:53.625
Here, Amanda.

00:11:53.625 --> 00:11:56.375
Thank you for teaching me.

00:11:56.375 --> 00:11:58.000
Oh, thank you.

00:11:58.000 --> 00:11:59.332
What is this?

00:11:59.332 --> 00:12:03.542
Super delicious curry. It's the king of all food!

00:12:05.625 --> 00:12:07.332
- Curry is the best!
- Where did she take that out from?

00:12:07.332 --> 00:12:10.625
- Here, Krad, have a meat sandwich.
- You're right! This is absolutely delicious!

00:12:10.625 --> 00:12:12.707
She is a fascinating character indeed.

00:12:12.707 --> 00:12:13.832
Indeed.

00:12:16.042 --> 00:12:19.457
Fran actually shared her curry with Amanda…

00:12:19.457 --> 00:12:23.375
Does that mean she trusts her now?

00:12:24.042 --> 00:12:27.207
(Reincarnated as a Sword)

00:12:27.207 --> 00:12:30.207
Are there other types of magic
besides the four elements?

00:12:30.207 --> 00:12:32.250
There is also light magic and dark magic.

00:12:32.250 --> 00:12:34.250
They're common among monsters,

00:12:34.250 --> 00:12:37.582
but they are mastered by even fewer people
than those who master complex magic.

00:12:38.500 --> 00:12:43.000
So we better don't let them know
that we can use both four elements and dark magic…

00:12:43.957 --> 00:12:46.542
From light stems
purification and illusion magic.

00:12:46.542 --> 00:12:50.917
From dark, you have poison
and necro magic and so on…

00:12:50.917 --> 00:12:52.082
Question.

00:12:52.082 --> 00:12:54.167
Yes, Fran?

00:12:54.167 --> 00:12:58.207
Are people who use poison and necro magic

00:12:58.207 --> 00:13:00.125
bad guys?

00:13:00.125 --> 00:13:02.917
They don't tend to give off the best impression,

00:13:02.917 --> 00:13:05.417
but a skill is only a skill.

00:13:05.417 --> 00:13:08.750
I know a necro mage myself.

00:13:08.750 --> 00:13:12.625
He certainly is
a rather shady and eccentric fellow…

00:13:12.625 --> 00:13:16.582
He must be really shady if even Amanda says so.

00:13:16.582 --> 00:13:20.042
Then, you also have your recovery magic
and summoning magic too.

00:13:20.042 --> 00:13:22.332
The more you travel,
the more you'll find in this world.

00:13:22.332 --> 00:13:25.207
Too much information…

00:13:25.207 --> 00:13:28.667
It must be hard for you to remember all of them.

00:13:28.667 --> 00:13:31.667
There are types of magic
that only monsters can use as well.

00:13:31.667 --> 00:13:32.917
Really?

00:13:32.917 --> 00:13:36.625
Monsters use magic
for their daily activities, after all.

00:13:36.625 --> 00:13:39.500
It's only natural
that they're more gifted in magic.

00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:42.417
I acquired my skills from monsters,

00:13:42.417 --> 00:13:46.125
so that's why I was able
to learn some rare magic and skills.

00:13:46.125 --> 00:13:48.375
In any case, that's all I know.

00:13:48.375 --> 00:13:52.292
Feel free to ask me
if you have any other questions.

00:13:52.292 --> 00:13:53.875
Thank you.

00:13:55.292 --> 00:13:56.707
This feels

00:13:56.707 --> 00:13:58.542
much easier than I expected.

00:13:58.542 --> 00:14:01.332
Is this really the promotion test?

00:14:01.332 --> 00:14:03.457
The fifth floor downward
is when things get serious.

00:14:03.457 --> 00:14:07.375
You'll be facing more monsters,
and some of them will even team up to attack.

00:14:07.375 --> 00:14:10.582
There'll be more kinds of traps too.

00:14:10.582 --> 00:14:13.792
Poisonous traps, trap holes…

00:14:13.792 --> 00:14:18.000
You might even run into the dangerous
Teleporter that forcibly teleports you away...

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:22.000
It's rare, but some have reportedly
been teleported into walls.

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:24.792
That sounds like a dangerous trap, indeed…

00:14:24.792 --> 00:14:27.332
People have also reported
encountering irregular ones

00:14:27.332 --> 00:14:32.792
like Directional Dyslexia
and Equipment Deactivation too.

00:14:33.792 --> 00:14:37.332
That is why you mustn't let your guard down.

00:14:37.332 --> 00:14:38.582
Teacher…

00:14:38.582 --> 00:14:40.292
What is it, Fran?

00:14:40.292 --> 00:14:41.750
Buzz, buzz!

00:14:42.792 --> 00:14:44.875
I want to learn thunder magic!

00:14:44.875 --> 00:14:48.125
No, no, no. You didn't even know
anything about complex magic until just now.

00:14:48.125 --> 00:14:50.542
It would definitely be suspicious
if you were able to use it all of a sudden.

00:14:50.542 --> 00:14:51.707
We'll learn it later.

00:14:53.167 --> 00:14:55.667
Later? When?

00:14:55.667 --> 00:14:57.417
- When?
- As I've explained…

00:14:57.417 --> 00:15:00.167
Please, Teacher! I really want
to use thunder magic and go buzz-buzz!

00:15:00.167 --> 00:15:02.707
- Buzz-buzz!
- Well…

00:15:02.707 --> 00:15:03.792
Can't I?

00:15:04.917 --> 00:15:06.875
Fine. You can learn it now,

00:15:06.875 --> 00:15:08.250
but you can't use it until we get back.

00:15:08.250 --> 00:15:10.332
You have to promise me that.

00:15:10.332 --> 00:15:13.167
Got it! Thank you, Teacher!

00:15:13.167 --> 00:15:16.582
Let's see… I have 47 self-evo points.

00:15:16.582 --> 00:15:19.042
Fire Magic is already at level 10.

00:15:19.042 --> 00:15:21.125
Let's max out Wind Magic too.

00:15:22.250 --> 00:15:25.125
Wind Magic has been increased to level 10.

00:15:25.125 --> 00:15:28.000
"Wind Mage" title acquired.

00:15:28.000 --> 00:15:31.707
New skill gained. Storm Magic 1.

00:15:31.707 --> 00:15:35.457
Both Fire Magic and Wind Magic
have reached level 10.

00:15:35.457 --> 00:15:38.625
New skill gained. Thunder Magic 1.

00:15:38.625 --> 00:15:40.542
All right. There you go.

00:15:40.542 --> 00:15:42.750
I've shared the skills via Skill Sharing.

00:15:42.750 --> 00:15:45.667
Yay! I can go buzz-buzz now!

00:15:45.667 --> 00:15:48.417
Let's practice them after we get back…

00:15:48.417 --> 00:15:50.375
Thunder Magic!

00:15:50.375 --> 00:15:53.542
- Stun…
- Stop that!

00:15:53.542 --> 00:15:55.042
(Dungeon Spider's Nest,
The Fifth Floor Underground)

00:15:55.042 --> 00:15:57.167
All right. Let's resume our investigation.

00:15:59.875 --> 00:16:02.542
I summon thee, Juran, the wood spirit!

00:16:02.542 --> 00:16:05.082
Please restrain the Trap Spiders

00:16:05.082 --> 00:16:08.000
but avoid my companions!

00:16:09.457 --> 00:16:14.542
So instead of chanting,
you make requests directly to spirits, huh...

00:16:14.542 --> 00:16:16.292
That sounds fun.

00:16:16.292 --> 00:16:18.500
There really are too many of them.

00:16:19.457 --> 00:16:21.292
This might turn into a melee.

00:16:21.292 --> 00:16:23.457
Don't let your guard down for even a second!

00:16:23.457 --> 00:16:25.542
I've been stabbed! I've been poisoned!

00:16:25.542 --> 00:16:27.292
What did I just say?

00:16:27.292 --> 00:16:29.042
Here's the antidote.

00:16:29.042 --> 00:16:30.375
Thank you!

00:16:30.375 --> 00:16:32.875
Do your best, everyone!

00:16:32.875 --> 00:16:34.832
And the trap on this floor…

00:16:36.417 --> 00:16:38.375
That'll take care of all the traps.

00:16:39.375 --> 00:16:42.750
That was a close call!
Did you do that on purpose?

00:16:42.750 --> 00:16:45.417
Can everyone still carry on?

00:16:45.417 --> 00:16:49.000
Of course! Don't underestimate the Dragon's Roar.

00:16:49.000 --> 00:16:51.707
The Forest Eyes can still proceed too.

00:16:51.707 --> 00:16:55.875
The dungeon core is located
in the deepest part of the sixth floor.

00:16:55.875 --> 00:16:59.042
We will withdraw once we retrieve the magic ore,

00:16:59.042 --> 00:17:02.542
and that will mark the end
of the investigation and the test.

00:17:02.542 --> 00:17:04.875
(Dungeon Spider's Nest,
The Sixth Floor Underground)

00:17:04.875 --> 00:17:07.000
We're completely surrounded.

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:09.583
Archers and mages,
please restrain the enemy moves!

00:17:09.583 --> 00:17:12.375
We'll clear the path!

00:17:13.541 --> 00:17:16.083
Be careful not to get poisoned!

00:17:16.083 --> 00:17:18.833
I feel like there are even more of them…

00:17:20.416 --> 00:17:22.208
Bring it on, you bastards!

00:17:24.702 --> 00:17:25.750
It didn't work…

00:17:25.750 --> 00:17:27.208
What's wrong?

00:17:27.208 --> 00:17:29.750
The antidote didn't work…

00:17:29.750 --> 00:17:31.541
What?

00:17:31.541 --> 00:17:33.041
Appraisal!

00:17:33.041 --> 00:17:35.375
Status. Deadly poison?

00:17:35.375 --> 00:17:37.750
Fran, that guy is badly poisoned.

00:17:37.750 --> 00:17:40.000
Cast recovery magic to heal him.

00:17:41.041 --> 00:17:44.291
Recovery Magic. Antidote.

00:17:45.333 --> 00:17:46.916
Angel…

00:17:48.583 --> 00:17:51.458
I've been cured! Thank… Thank you!

00:17:52.750 --> 00:17:56.166
This is strange.
The spiders seem to have become a lot tougher.

00:17:56.166 --> 00:17:57.708
Teacher.

00:17:57.708 --> 00:18:00.458
Let's use Appraisal, just in case.

00:18:00.458 --> 00:18:04.125
(Trick Spider, Lv. 10)
So that's what they are.

00:18:04.125 --> 00:18:07.708
These are the evolved forms
of Trap Spiders. They're Trick Spiders.

00:18:07.708 --> 00:18:10.083
They're an evolved form
that can inject deadly poison!

00:18:10.083 --> 00:18:11.916
Be careful, everyone!

00:18:11.916 --> 00:18:13.500
Seriously?

00:18:13.500 --> 00:18:15.250
According to info from the guild,

00:18:15.250 --> 00:18:18.375
only Trap Spiders would spawn periodically.

00:18:20.291 --> 00:18:23.083
They are not supposed to
spawn again in a cleared dungeon!

00:18:23.083 --> 00:18:26.041
Don't tell me they've evolved by themselves!

00:18:26.041 --> 00:18:28.750
Given their numbers,

00:18:28.750 --> 00:18:31.958
this is too much for E-rank parties to handle.

00:18:34.375 --> 00:18:37.291
Dragon's Roar! Forest Eyes! Fall back!

00:18:37.291 --> 00:18:39.375
Retreat to the fifth floor!

00:18:39.375 --> 00:18:42.375
You can't be serious!
We've already come this far…

00:18:44.041 --> 00:18:46.250
Bart! Victor!

00:18:46.250 --> 00:18:48.083
Fire Arrow!

00:18:48.916 --> 00:18:50.833
Miss Amanda! Miss Fran!

00:18:50.833 --> 00:18:52.416
Please clear a path for us to withdraw!

00:18:53.208 --> 00:18:54.541
Okay.

00:18:56.416 --> 00:18:58.833
Whip Technique. Lion Chain!

00:18:58.833 --> 00:19:00.958
Sonic Wave!

00:19:00.958 --> 00:19:03.166
All right! Retreat for now!

00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:12.375
There are spiders here too!

00:19:12.375 --> 00:19:14.250
They're coming this way!

00:19:18.916 --> 00:19:20.416
Those two

00:19:20.416 --> 00:19:22.000
have been struck by Confusion Toxin.

00:19:22.000 --> 00:19:22.958
What…

00:19:23.916 --> 00:19:25.458
Stop!

00:19:25.458 --> 00:19:27.291
Let's escape through there!

00:19:27.291 --> 00:19:28.833
All right!

00:19:28.833 --> 00:19:32.416
Wait! I haven't used Trap Detection in that zone!

00:19:36.583 --> 00:19:37.833
Fran!

00:19:38.375 --> 00:19:40.666
Fran, are you all right?

00:19:41.458 --> 00:19:42.916
I was careless…

00:19:42.916 --> 00:19:44.916
Good grief, these two…

00:19:46.458 --> 00:19:47.458
What?

00:19:47.458 --> 00:19:48.583
Teacher!

00:19:48.583 --> 00:19:50.500
Mana flow…

00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:51.875
Don't tell me it's…

00:19:51.875 --> 00:19:53.583
It's Teleporter!

00:19:53.583 --> 00:19:54.625
Fran!

00:19:54.625 --> 00:19:56.625
T… Teacher!

00:19:56.625 --> 00:19:59.500
It's okay. Grab onto me.

00:19:59.500 --> 00:20:01.250
As long as we don't get teleported into a wall,

00:20:01.250 --> 00:20:02.958
I'll get us out!

00:20:02.958 --> 00:20:04.416
I will…

00:20:11.875 --> 00:20:14.958
No way… Is this…

00:20:14.958 --> 00:20:19.625
A complex trap of Teleporter and Weapon Disarm?

00:20:19.625 --> 00:20:22.916
Why would there be such a high-level trap
in a cleared dungeon?

00:20:22.916 --> 00:20:25.041
Damn it! My party members have been…

00:20:25.041 --> 00:20:27.958
Eizelle! Do you know
where they've been teleported to?

00:20:27.958 --> 00:20:29.583
According to the map from the guild,

00:20:29.583 --> 00:20:31.875
they should've been teleported
into a small room nearby.

00:20:31.875 --> 00:20:33.291
Let's hurry there.

00:20:36.125 --> 00:20:39.208
Victor! Bart! Wait for me!

00:20:40.375 --> 00:20:41.500
Fran!

00:20:43.208 --> 00:20:44.500
They're not here.

00:20:44.500 --> 00:20:46.541
This can't be…

00:20:46.541 --> 00:20:49.500
Does this mean
the teleport destination has been altered?

00:20:49.500 --> 00:20:51.750
But this shouldn't be possible

00:20:51.750 --> 00:20:53.583
without a Dungeon Master…

00:20:53.583 --> 00:20:55.041
No.

00:20:56.250 --> 00:20:58.958
There is one other possibility.

00:21:05.916 --> 00:21:07.500
Teacher…

00:21:10.166 --> 00:21:11.583
Teacher…

00:21:11.583 --> 00:21:13.416
No way…

00:21:13.416 --> 00:21:15.250
There's something over there…

00:21:15.250 --> 00:21:16.833
It's massive…

00:21:17.750 --> 00:21:21.083
Miss Amanda, what is that possibility?

00:21:21.916 --> 00:21:23.916
There is a monster that is capable

00:21:23.916 --> 00:21:27.125
of setting and altering traps…

00:21:28.791 --> 00:21:31.333
The Trick Spider's final evolved form…

00:21:32.250 --> 00:21:34.291
A Trickster Spider!

00:21:38.875 --> 00:21:40.708
Without Teacher,

00:21:40.708 --> 00:21:43.625
I can't use skills or magic…

00:21:43.625 --> 00:21:49.375
Echolocation!
Presence Detection! Heat Detection!

00:21:49.375 --> 00:21:51.875
None of them is working!

00:21:51.875 --> 00:21:55.083
I can't find her with any of the skills I have!

00:21:55.083 --> 00:21:57.833
Fran, where are you?

00:21:57.833 --> 00:21:59.833
Where are you?

00:21:59.833 --> 00:22:01.833
Answer me!

00:23:34.375 --> 00:23:40.125
(Next Episode
Summoning the Demon Wolf)
